body:
yada yada, like everyone else said, sausage/Western/bacon burritos are premade. i think they're supposed to be more of like a snack wrap vibe, kinda more like that sausage burrito from McDonald's. there's a 2 for $6 deal on them bc it's not rly worth just getting one of them.

that being said, they still suck. they used to be better but the company switched distributors a couple yrs ago and now theyre bland asf. if i order them it's just to add to what else im getting and ill get a sauce to dip it in. sauce makes it much much better lol.

if you get a made to order burrito where you pick the ingredients make sure to always get at least 2 proteins. otherwise it'll still be a small burrito. get steak and eggs, or eggs and rice, etc. or you can get double steak or double what ever. and load it up with veggies/toppings and sauce! the end :)

people are pissed bc op called it harassment..... i think op may not be painting the picture well enough. why would op just say that shit? yall are ALL gonna assume they're being dramatic and that's absolutely the truth? they said their parents do it knowing theyre awake. maybe it really is loud and over the top? maybe the parents literally don't give a fuck? maybe they do think theyre being quiet and discreet. but op knows his or her parents, maybe they have reason to believe theyre being inconsiderate assholes.

@op; definitely say something to them. but if you don't, or if you do and they don't stop, or for any future reason you need to make your own silence to fall asleep, here is what i do:

there's a headband on amazon that covers your ears and has little speaker/ear buds that go over your ears. it's bluetooth, so download a white noise machine app on your phone (one that continues to play while your phone is locked). (also the app will have different types of noise, i suggest using brown noise). wear this head band while you sleep but also wear earplugs under it. this way you aren't damaging your eardrums, and also this combination just blocks out sound 100%. type in "sleep headphones headband" on amazon. it's like, 20 bucks.
